# Store every text file with LF line endings, whatever the checkout platform.
#
# Without this, files edited on Windows with core.autocrlf unset were written
# back with CRLF and sat permanently "modified" in git status — equal insertion
# and deletion counts, byte-identical content — which made a real review of
# those files impossible. `text=auto` lets git decide what is text; `eol=lf`
# keeps the working copy LF too, which every tool this project uses is happy
# with (and which matches what CI checks out on Linux).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.apkg binary
*.wasm binary
